bove?" :question/worked-solution "Every inequality can be expressed as an interval. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses $()$ if the endpoints are *not* included.\n\n- Brackets $[]$ if the endpoints *are* included.\n\nThe given interval can be represented by the following inequality:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\,\\le \\,\\,x\\,\\,<\\,\\,4\n$$\n\nWe can express our inequality in interval notation as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\in [2,4)\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Translating Between Half-Open Intervals and Number Lines"}
